# TODO - Static reference ledger and research retention

## Objective

Use a function-first static analysis workflow and bounded investigation
retention for all selected titles; keep original software and its
decompiler output private.

## Acceptance

- Prefer a verified Ghidra processor and loader for each selected lawful
  binary. Record the exact edition, tool revision, CPU, address spaces,
  bank mapping, executable regions and analysis limitations. Use other
  appropriate static tools when the required processor is unavailable;
  never interpret one instruction set as another.
- Keep one durable private per-title JSON Lines function inventory in
  `.reference/games/<title>/ledger.jsonl`. Give each function a stable
  identity comprising module, CPU, address space or bank, and entry
  address; preserve the original FUN identifier or symbol.
- Record semantic name, inputs, outputs, state mutations, callers,
  callees, data dependencies, confidence, Rust owner and symbol,
  test evidence and status. Reconcile function discovery, indirect
  calls and unexplained executable regions; separate data from code.
- Resolve every discovered function as implemented, shared mechanism,
  intentional documented replacement, non-runtime or unresolved.
  Do not treat an unclassified address or guessed behavior as complete.
  Use verified semantic specifications for independent Rust
  implementation; do not publish original pseudocode or proprietary
  code. Preserve existing importer, IR, safety and licensing boundaries.
- Use targeted emulator observations for ambiguities, assets and
  regression tests. Do not repeat broad visual experiments in place
  of static analysis. Measure progress by resolved functions and
  playable campaign milestones, not capture counts or commits.
- Provide a bounded research retention guard through contributor
  tooling. Keep disposable captures in a dedicated scratch namespace.
  Record the retained evidence, reproduction inputs and completion
  status before making a run eligible for removal.
- Default to read-only inventory and cleanup preview; require explicit
  application of a bounded plan. Apply age and size retention only to
  positively identified completed, archived and regenerable runs.
  Reject unsafe paths, links, active or unclassified investigations.
  Protect originals, tool installations, private analysis projects,
  durable ledgers and canonical assets. Test with tiny scratch fixtures.
- Keep unclassified historical captures until individually reviewed.
  Document reclaimed bytes and retained evidence; never delete an
  investigation merely because it is old.

## Evidence

